-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 12: expert evidence.  Part roc2, layer 1.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT: see roc2-order-9a.l4 and NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (roc2)").
-- Every answer is subject to O 3 r 2(1) (roc1): the Court's discretion to order otherwise.
-- The count of a period is O 3 r 3 (roc1): a period function takes `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 12, Rule 1 -- expert`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1180 | 1. —(1) An expert is a person with scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge based on training, study or experience. (2) An expert has the duty to assist the Court in the matters within his or her expertise and on the issues referred to him or her.
@ref O 12 r 1(1) (src:1180)
GIVEN `the person has scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that knowledge is based on training, study or experience` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 1(1) a person is an expert` MEANS
    IF `the person has scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge` AND `that knowledge is based on training, study or experience`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An expert is a person with scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge based on training, study or experience" (a definition that says "is")

-- src:1180 | 1. —(1) An expert is a person with scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge based on training, study or experience. (2) An expert has the duty to assist the Court in the matters within his or her expertise and on the issues referred to him or her.
@ref O 12 r 1(2) (src:1180)
GIVEN `the person is an expert` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is within the expert's expertise and on the issues referred to the expert` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 1(2) the expert has the duty to assist the Court on the matter` MEANS
    IF `the person is an expert` AND `the matter is within the expert's expertise and on the issues referred to the expert`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the matters within his or her expertise and on the issues referred to him or her"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1181 | (3) The expert’s duty to the Court overrides any obligation to the person from whom the expert receives instructions or by whom the expert is paid.
@ref O 12 r 1(3) (src:1181)
GIVEN `the obligation is owed to the person from whom the expert receives instructions or by whom the expert is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 1(3) the expert's duty to the Court overrides the obligation` MEANS
    IF `the obligation is owed to the person from whom the expert receives instructions or by whom the expert is paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any obligation to the person from whom the expert receives instructions or by whom the expert is paid"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 12, Rule 2 -- Court to approve use of expert evidence`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1183 | 2. —(1) No expert evidence may be used in Court unless the Court approves. (2) The parties must consider whether expert evidence will contribute materially to the determination of any issue that relates to scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge and whether such issue can be resolved by an agreed statement of facts or by submissions based on mutually agreed materials.
@ref O 12 r 2(1) (src:1183)
GIVEN `the Court approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 2(1) expert evidence may be used in Court` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Court approves`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No expert evidence may be used in Court unless the Court approves" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for evidence used "unless the Court approves"; with approval paragraphs (3) and (4) decide [marginal-b]

-- src:1183 | 2. —(1) No expert evidence may be used in Court unless the Court approves. (2) The parties must consider whether expert evidence will contribute materially to the determination of any issue that relates to scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge and whether such issue can be resolved by an agreed statement of facts or by submissions based on mutually agreed materials.
@ref O 12 r 2(2) (src:1183)
GIVEN `the parties have considered whether expert evidence will contribute materially to the determination of any issue that relates to scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties have considered whether such issue can be resolved by an agreed statement of facts or by submissions based on mutually agreed materials` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 2(2) the parties have considered what paragraph (2) requires` MEANS
    IF `the parties have considered whether expert evidence will contribute materially to the determination of any issue that relates to scientific, technical or other specialised knowledge` AND `the parties have considered whether such issue can be resolved by an agreed statement of facts or by submissions based on mutually agreed materials`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The parties must consider whether expert evidence will contribute materially ... and whether such issue can be resolved by an agreed statement of facts or by submissions based on mutually agreed materials" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:1184 | (3) The Court must not approve the use of expert evidence unless it will contribute materially to the determination of any issue in the case and the issue cannot be resolved in the manner stated in paragraph (2).
@ref O 12 r 2(3) (src:1184)
GIVEN `expert evidence will contribute materially to the determination of any issue in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issue can be resolved by an agreed statement of facts or by submissions based on mutually agreed materials` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 2(3) the Court may approve the use of expert evidence` MEANS
    IF (NOT `expert evidence will contribute materially to the determination of any issue in the case`) OR `the issue can be resolved by an agreed statement of facts or by submissions based on mutually agreed materials`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Court must not approve the use of expert evidence unless it will contribute materially to the determination of any issue in the case and the issue cannot be resolved in the manner stated in paragraph (2)" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for approval "unless" both conditions are met; when they are, paragraph (3) does not itself give the approval [marginal-b]

-- src:1185 | (4) The Court may disallow the use of or reject any expert evidence if it is of the opinion that the expert lacks the requisite specialised knowledge in the issues referred to him or her or that he or she lacks impartiality.
@ref O 12 r 2(4) (src:1185)
GIVEN `the Court is of the opinion that the expert lacks the requisite specialised knowledge in the issues referred to the expert` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is of the opinion that the expert lacks impartiality` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 2(4) the Court may disallow the use of or reject the expert evidence` MEANS
    IF `the Court is of the opinion that the expert lacks the requisite specialised knowledge in the issues referred to the expert` OR `the Court is of the opinion that the expert lacks impartiality`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is of the opinion that the expert lacks the requisite specialised knowledge ... or that he or she lacks impartiality" (an "if" that fails, reading (a) of the rule of 2026-10-29) [marginal-a]

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 12, Rule 3 -- common expert, court expert and number of experts`
-- ===========================================================================

-- Paragraph (5) is asked first: it takes paragraphs (1) to (4) away, and paragraph (1) is "subject to paragraph (5)".
-- src:1190 | (5) Paragraphs (1) to (4) do not apply to any proceedings before a Magistrate’s Court or District Court where any question requiring the evidence of an expert witness arises in a case which the Court has directed to be set down for a simplified trial, and instead — ( a )
@ref O 12 r 3(5) (src:1190)
GIVEN level IS A `Court level`
      `a question requiring the evidence of an expert witness arises in a case which the Court has directed to be set down for a simplified trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 3(5) paragraph (5) applies to the proceedings` MEANS
    (level EQUALS `Magistrate's Court` OR level EQUALS `District Court`) AND `a question requiring the evidence of an expert witness arises in a case which the Court has directed to be set down for a simplified trial`

-- src:1190 | (5) Paragraphs (1) to (4) do not apply to any proceedings before a Magistrate’s Court or District Court where any question requiring the evidence of an expert witness arises in a case which the Court has directed to be set down for a simplified trial, and instead — ( a )
@ref O 12 r 3(5) (src:1190)
GIVEN `paragraph (5) applies to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 3(5) paragraphs (1) to (4) apply to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (5) applies to the proceedings`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraphs (1) to (4) do not apply to any proceedings before a Magistrate's Court or District Court where ... a simplified trial"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (5) takes paragraphs (1) to (4) away only for those proceedings; for others they apply of their own force

-- src:1187 | 3. —(1) Subject to paragraph (5), as far as possible, parties must agree on one common expert. (2) Except in a special case and with the Court’s approval, a party may not rely on expert evidence from more than one expert for any issue.
@ref O 12 r 3(1) (src:1187)
GIVEN `paragraph (5) applies to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is possible for the parties to agree on one common expert` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 3(1) the parties must agree on one common expert` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (5) applies to the proceedings`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraph (5)": paragraph (5) says paragraphs (1) to (4) do not apply
    ELSE
        IF `it is possible for the parties to agree on one common expert`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as far as possible"; where it is not possible the Rule does not say what follows [marginal-b]

-- Fork F-O12-1: "Except in a special case and with the Court's approval" is read as BOTH conditions together.
-- src:1187 | 3. —(1) Subject to paragraph (5), as far as possible, parties must agree on one common expert. (2) Except in a special case and with the Court’s approval, a party may not rely on expert evidence from more than one expert for any issue.
@ref O 12 r 3(2) (src:1187)
GIVEN `paragraph (5) applies to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 3(2) the party may rely on expert evidence from more than one expert for the issue` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (5) applies to the proceedings`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph (5) says paragraphs (1) to (4) do not apply, so paragraph (2) gives the party nothing here
    ELSE
        IF NOT (`it is a special case` AND `the Court approves`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except in a special case and with the Court's approval, a party may not rely on expert evidence from more than one expert for any issue" (flat negative, ruling N2)
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for the case that is not both "a special case" and "with the Court's approval"; inside the exception paragraph (2) is silent [marginal-b]

DECLARE `o 12 r 3(3) a court expert` IS ONE OF
    `o 12 r 3(3) in addition to the parties' common expert`
    `o 12 r 3(3) in place of the parties' common expert`
    `o 12 r 3(3) in place of all the experts`

-- src:1188 | (3) In a special case, the Court may appoint a court expert in addition to or in place of the parties’ common expert or all the experts.
@ref O 12 r 3(3) (src:1188)
GIVEN `paragraph (5) applies to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN
      appointment IS A `o 12 r 3(3) a court expert`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 3(3) the Court may appoint a court expert` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (5) applies to the proceedings`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph (5) says paragraphs (1) to (4) do not apply
    ELSE
        IF `it is a special case`
        THEN
            CONSIDER appointment
            WHEN `o 12 r 3(3) in addition to the parties' common expert` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `o 12 r 3(3) in place of the parties' common expert` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `o 12 r 3(3) in place of all the experts` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In a special case"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

DECLARE `o 12 r 3(4) a matter` IS ONE OF
    `o 12 r 3(4) the appointment of experts`
    `o 12 r 3(4) the method of questioning in Court`
    `o 12 r 3(4) the remuneration to be paid to the experts`

-- src:1189 | (4) The Court must give all appropriate directions relating to the appointment of experts, including the method of questioning in Court and the remuneration to be paid to them.
@ref O 12 r 3(4) (src:1189)
GIVEN `paragraph (5) applies to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `o 12 r 3(4) a matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 3(4) the Court must give all appropriate directions on this matter` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (5) applies to the proceedings`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph (5) says paragraphs (1) to (4) do not apply
    ELSE
        CONSIDER matter
        WHEN `o 12 r 3(4) the appointment of experts` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 12 r 3(4) the method of questioning in Court` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 12 r 3(4) the remuneration to be paid to the experts` THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:1190 | (5) Paragraphs (1) to (4) do not apply to any proceedings before a Magistrate’s Court or District Court where any question requiring the evidence of an expert witness arises in a case which the Court has directed to be set down for a simplified trial, and instead — ( a )
