§ `Order 12, Rule 4 -- issues and common set of facts`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1202 | 4. —(1) The parties must agree on the list of issues to be referred for expert evidence and the common set of agreed or assumed facts that the experts are to rely on. (2) The list of issues and the common set of agreed or assumed facts must be approved by the Court and unless the Court otherwise orders, the expert evidence must be confined to the approved issues and must rely on the common set of agreed or assumed facts only.
@ref O 12 r 4(1) (src:1202)
GIVEN `the parties have agreed on the list of issues to be referred for expert evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties have agreed on the common set of agreed or assumed facts that the experts are to rely on` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 4(1) the parties have agreed on what paragraph (1) requires` MEANS
    IF `the parties have agreed on the list of issues to be referred for expert evidence` AND `the parties have agreed on the common set of agreed or assumed facts that the experts are to rely on`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The parties must agree on the list of issues ... and the common set of agreed or assumed facts" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:1202 | 4. —(1) The parties must agree on the list of issues to be referred for expert evidence and the common set of agreed or assumed facts that the experts are to rely on. (2) The list of issues and the common set of agreed or assumed facts must be approved by the Court and unless the Court otherwise orders, the expert evidence must be confined to the approved issues and must rely on the common set of agreed or assumed facts only.
@ref O 12 r 4(2) (src:1202)
GIVEN `the Court has approved the list of issues and the common set of agreed or assumed facts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 4(2) the list of issues and the common set of agreed or assumed facts are approved` MEANS
    IF `the Court has approved the list of issues and the common set of agreed or assumed facts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be approved by the Court" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:1202 | 4. —(1) The parties must agree on the list of issues to be referred for expert evidence and the common set of agreed or assumed facts that the experts are to rely on. (2) The list of issues and the common set of agreed or assumed facts must be approved by the Court and unless the Court otherwise orders, the expert evidence must be confined to the approved issues and must rely on the common set of agreed or assumed facts only.
@ref O 12 r 4(2) (src:1202)
GIVEN `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expert evidence is confined to the approved issues` IS A BOOLEAN
