GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 4(2) the expert evidence is confined as required` MEANS
    IF `the Court otherwise orders`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the Court otherwise orders"; what the Court orders is for the order [marginal-b]
    ELSE
        IF `the expert evidence is confined to the approved issues` AND `the expert evidence relies on the common set of agreed or assumed facts only`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the expert evidence must be confined to the approved issues and must rely on the common set of agreed or assumed facts only" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:1203 | (3) If there is no agreement as mentioned in paragraph (1), the Court must decide the list of issues and the common set of agreed or assumed facts.
