GIVEN `there is no agreement as mentioned in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 4(3) the Court must decide the list of issues and the common set of agreed or assumed facts` MEANS
    IF `there is no agreement as mentioned in paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If there is no agreement as mentioned in paragraph (1)" fails [marginal-a]

-- src:1204 | (4) As far as possible, the issues must be expressed in the form of questions which can be answered with “yes” or “no”.
@ref O 12 r 4(4) (src:1204)
GIVEN `it is possible to express the issue in the form of a question which can be answered with yes or no` IS A BOOLEAN
