GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 4(4) the issue is expressed as required` MEANS
    IF `it is possible to express the issue in the form of a question which can be answered with yes or no`
    THEN
        IF `the issue is expressed in that form`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the issues must be expressed in the form of questions which can be answered with “yes” or “no”" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "As far as possible"; where it is not possible the Rule does not say what follows [marginal-b]

