`o 12 r 5(1) the expert evidence is given as required` MEANS
    IF `the report is signed by the expert` AND `the report is exhibited in an affidavit made by the expert`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Expert evidence must be given in a report signed by the expert and exhibited in an affidavit made by the expert" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- Limbs (a) to (h) of paragraph (2).  A limb that asks for nothing on the facts (limbs (e) and (f)) is met: nothing is missing from the report.
