    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The expert's report must include" (b) (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:1210 | ( c )
-- src:1211 | the issues referred to the expert and the common set of agreed or assumed facts that he or she relied on;
@ref O 12 r 5(2)(c) (src:1210-1211)
GIVEN `the report includes the issues referred to the expert and the common set of agreed or assumed facts that the expert relied on` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 5(2)(c) the report includes the issues and the common set of facts` MEANS
    IF `the report includes the issues referred to the expert and the common set of agreed or assumed facts that the expert relied on`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The expert's report must include" (c) (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:1212 | ( d )
-- src:1213 | a list of the materials that the expert relied on and including only extracts of the materials which are necessary to understand the report;
@ref O 12 r 5(2)(d) (src:1212-1213)
GIVEN `the report includes a list of the materials that the expert relied on` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes only extracts of the materials which are necessary to understand the report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 5(2)(d) the report includes a list of the materials relied on` MEANS
    IF `the report includes a list of the materials that the expert relied on` AND `the report includes only extracts of the materials which are necessary to understand the report`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The expert's report must include" (d) (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:1214 | ( e )
-- src:1215 | where the materials include tests, experiments or the collection or analysis of data, the names and qualifications of the persons who did the tests, experiments or the collection or analysis of data and whether they did so under the expert’s supervision or guidance;
@ref O 12 r 5(2)(e) (src:1214-1215)
GIVEN `the materials include tests, experiments or the collection or analysis of data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes the names and qualifications of the persons who did them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether they did so under the expert's supervision or guidance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 5(2)(e) the report includes the names and qualifications of those who did the tests` MEANS
    IF NOT `the materials include tests, experiments or the collection or analysis of data`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the limb asks for nothing where the materials include no tests, experiments or data: "where the materials include" [marginal-a]
    ELSE
        IF `the report includes the names and qualifications of the persons who did them` AND `the report states whether they did so under the expert's supervision or guidance`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The expert's report must include" (e) (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:1216 | ( f )
-- src:1217 | where there is a range of opinion on the matters dealt with in the report — (i)
-- src:1218 | a summary of the range of opinion; and
-- src:1219 | (ii)
-- src:1220 | the reasons for the expert’s opinion;
@ref O 12 r 5(2)(f) (src:1216-1220)
GIVEN `there is a range of opinion on the matters dealt with in the report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes a summary of the range of opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report includes the reasons for the expert's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 5(2)(f) the report includes a summary of the range of opinion and the reasons` MEANS
    IF NOT `there is a range of opinion on the matters dealt with in the report`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the limb asks for nothing where there is no range of opinion: "where there is a range of opinion" [marginal-a]
    ELSE
        IF `the report includes a summary of the range of opinion` AND `the report includes the reasons for the expert's opinion`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The expert's report must include" (f) (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:1221 | ( g )
-- src:1222 | a statement of belief of correctness of the expert’s opinion;
@ref O 12 r 5(2)(g) (src:1221-1222)
GIVEN `the report includes a statement of belief of correctness of the expert's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 5(2)(g) the report includes a statement of belief of correctness` MEANS
    IF `the report includes a statement of belief of correctness of the expert's opinion`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The expert's report must include" (g) (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:1223 | ( h )
-- src:1224 | the conclusions reached on the issues referred to the expert and the reasons to support the conclusions.
@ref O 12 r 5(2)(h) (src:1223-1224)
GIVEN `the report includes the conclusions reached on the issues referred to the expert and the reasons to support the conclusions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 5(2)(h) the report includes the conclusions and the reasons` MEANS
    IF `the report includes the conclusions reached on the issues referred to the expert and the reasons to support the conclusions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The expert's report must include" (h) (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:1206 | 5. —(1) Expert evidence must be given in a report signed by the expert and exhibited in an affidavit made by the expert. (2) The expert’s report must include the following: ( a )
-- src:1207 | the expert’s qualifications showing that he or she has the requisite specialised knowledge on the issues referred to him or her;
-- src:1208 | ( b )
-- src:1209 | the expert’s statement that he or she understands his or her duty is to assist the Court in the matters within his or her expertise and on the issues referred to him or her and that such duty to the Court overrides any obligation to the person from whom he or she receives instructions or by whom he or she is paid;
-- src:1210 | ( c )
-- src:1211 | the issues referred to the expert and the common set of agreed or assumed facts that he or she relied on;
-- src:1212 | ( d )
-- src:1213 | a list of the materials that the expert relied on and including only extracts of the materials which are necessary to understand the report;
-- src:1214 | ( e )
-- src:1215 | where the materials include tests, experiments or the collection or analysis of data, the names and qualifications of the persons who did the tests, experiments or the collection or analysis of data and whether they did so under the expert’s supervision or guidance;
-- src:1216 | ( f )
-- src:1217 | where there is a range of opinion on the matters dealt with in the report — (i)
-- src:1218 | a summary of the range of opinion; and
-- src:1219 | (ii)
-- src:1220 | the reasons for the expert’s opinion;
-- src:1221 | ( g )
-- src:1222 | a statement of belief of correctness of the expert’s opinion;
-- src:1223 | ( h )
-- src:1224 | the conclusions reached on the issues referred to the expert and the reasons to support the conclusions.
@ref O 12 r 5(2) (src:1206-1224)
GIVEN `limb (a) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (b) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (c) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (d) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (e) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (f) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (g) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (h) answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 5(2) the expert's report includes what paragraph (2) requires` MEANS
    IF `limb (a) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `limb (b) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `limb (c) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `limb (d) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `limb (e) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `limb (f) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `limb (g) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `limb (h) answers` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE
        IF `limb (a) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `limb (b) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `limb (c) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `limb (d) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `limb (e) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `limb (f) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `limb (g) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `limb (h) answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The expert's report must include the following": at least one limb is not met (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a limb is not covered, so the gathered answer is not covered

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 12, Rule 6 -- meeting, clarification on report and cross-examination`
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `o 12 r 6(1) a time of the meeting` IS ONE OF
    `o 12 r 6(1) before the making of the expert reports`
    `o 12 r 6(1) during the making of the expert reports`
    `o 12 r 6(1) after the making of the expert reports`

-- src:1226 | 6. —(1) The Court may order the parties, their solicitors and the experts to meet before, during or after the making of the expert reports to try to narrow any dispute and so that the parties can agree in writing on all or some of the conclusions on the issues referred to the experts. (2) Other than the contents of any agreement in writing, the contents of discussions at a meeting mentioned in paragraph (1) must not be used in Court unless the parties otherwise agree.
@ref O 12 r 6(1) (src:1226)
GIVEN time IS A `o 12 r 6(1) a time of the meeting`
      `the meeting is to try to narrow any dispute and so that the parties can agree in writing on all or some of the conclusions on the issues referred to the experts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 6(1) the Court may order the parties, their solicitors and the experts to meet` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is to try to narrow any dispute and so that the parties can agree in writing on all or some of the conclusions on the issues referred to the experts`
    THEN
        CONSIDER time
        WHEN `o 12 r 6(1) before the making of the expert reports` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 12 r 6(1) during the making of the expert reports` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 12 r 6(1) after the making of the expert reports` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given "to try to narrow any dispute"; for another purpose the Rule does not say [marginal-b]

-- src:1226 | 6. —(1) The Court may order the parties, their solicitors and the experts to meet before, during or after the making of the expert reports to try to narrow any dispute and so that the parties can agree in writing on all or some of the conclusions on the issues referred to the experts. (2) Other than the contents of any agreement in writing, the contents of discussions at a meeting mentioned in paragraph (1) must not be used in Court unless the parties otherwise agree.
@ref O 12 r 6(2) (src:1226)
GIVEN `it is the content of an agreement in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the content of discussions at a meeting mentioned in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties otherwise agree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 6(2) the content may be used in Court` MEANS
    IF `it is the content of discussions at a meeting mentioned in paragraph (1)` AND (NOT `it is the content of an agreement in writing`) AND (NOT `the parties otherwise agree`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Other than the contents of any agreement in writing, the contents of discussions at a meeting mentioned in paragraph (1) must not be used in Court unless the parties otherwise agree" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for the contents of discussions, other than a written agreement, "unless the parties otherwise agree"; outside it paragraph (2) is silent [marginal-b]

-- src:1227 | (3) With the Court’s approval, the parties may request in writing that an expert clarify his or her report in any aspect.
@ref O 12 r 6(3) (src:1227)
GIVEN `the Court approves` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 6(3) the parties may request the expert to clarify the report in any aspect` MEANS
    IF `the Court approves` AND `the request is in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "With the Court's approval, the parties may request in writing"; the text does not say no without them [marginal-b]

-- src:1228 | (4) Upon receipt of a request mentioned in paragraph (3), the expert must give his or her clarification in writing within the time specified by the Court and such clarification is deemed to be part of his or her report.
@ref O 12 r 6(4) (src:1228)
GIVEN `the expert receives a request mentioned in paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 6(4) the expert must give the clarification in writing` MEANS
    IF `the expert receives a request mentioned in paragraph (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon receipt of a request mentioned in paragraph (3)" fails (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- The time is "the time specified by the Court": no number of days in the Rule, so no regulative rule; the last day is O 3 r 3's (roc1).
-- src:1228 | (4) Upon receipt of a request mentioned in paragraph (3), the expert must give his or her clarification in writing within the time specified by the Court and such clarification is deemed to be part of his or her report.
@ref O 12 r 6(4) (src:1228)
GIVEN `the clarification is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the expert gives the clarification` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 6(4) the expert gives the clarification in writing in time` MEANS
    IF `the clarification is in writing` AND `the date the expert gives the clarification` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must give his or her clarification in writing within the time specified by the Court" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md; a period the Court specifies, ruling of 2026-11-05, (a)) [marginal-c]

-- src:1228 | (4) Upon receipt of a request mentioned in paragraph (3), the expert must give his or her clarification in writing within the time specified by the Court and such clarification is deemed to be part of his or her report.
@ref O 12 r 6(4) (src:1228)
GIVEN `it is a clarification given under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 6(4) the clarification is part of the expert's report` MEANS
    IF `it is a clarification given under paragraph (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such clarification is deemed to be part of his or her report"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1229 | (5) The parties must consider whether the experts need to be cross‑examined in Court.
@ref O 12 r 6(5) (src:1229)
GIVEN `the parties have considered whether the experts need to be cross-examined in Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 6(5) the parties have considered whether the experts need to be cross-examined` MEANS
    IF `the parties have considered whether the experts need to be cross-examined in Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The parties must consider whether the experts need to be cross-examined in Court" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 12, Rule 7 -- panel of experts`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:1231 | 7. —(1) In a case where there is more than one expert, the Court may order that all or some of the experts testify as a panel. (2) The panel of experts may testify before or after all or some of the non‑expert witnesses have testified.
@ref O 12 r 7(1) (src:1231)
GIVEN `there is more than one expert in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 7(1) the Court may order that all or some of the experts testify as a panel` MEANS
    IF `there is more than one expert in the case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In a case where there is more than one expert" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

DECLARE `o 12 r 7(2) a time` IS ONE OF
    `o 12 r 7(2) before all or some of the non-expert witnesses have testified`
    `o 12 r 7(2) after all or some of the non-expert witnesses have testified`

-- src:1231 | 7. —(1) In a case where there is more than one expert, the Court may order that all or some of the experts testify as a panel. (2) The panel of experts may testify before or after all or some of the non‑expert witnesses have testified.
@ref O 12 r 7(2) (src:1231)
GIVEN `the experts testify as a panel` IS A BOOLEAN
      time IS A `o 12 r 7(2) a time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 7(2) the panel of experts may testify at this time` MEANS
    IF `the experts testify as a panel`
    THEN
        CONSIDER time
        WHEN `o 12 r 7(2) before all or some of the non-expert witnesses have testified` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 12 r 7(2) after all or some of the non-expert witnesses have testified` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The panel of experts"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1232 | (3) If the defendant’s expert testifies as a panel before the defendant or any of the defendant’s non‑expert witnesses has testified, the defendant is not deemed to have waived his or her right to submit that there is no case for him or her to answer at that stage of the hearing.
@ref O 12 r 7(3) (src:1232)
GIVEN `the defendant's expert testifies as a panel before the defendant or any of the defendant's non-expert witnesses has testified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 7(3) the defendant is deemed to have waived the right to submit that there is no case to answer at that stage` MEANS
    IF `the defendant's expert testifies as a panel before the defendant or any of the defendant's non-expert witnesses has testified`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the defendant is not deemed to have waived his or her right to submit that there is no case for him or her to answer at that stage of the hearing" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of the defendant's expert testifying as a panel before the defendant or any non-expert witness has testified; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

DECLARE `o 12 r 7(4) a thing the panel might be ordered to do` IS ONE OF
    `o 12 r 7(4) give their views on the issues referred to them`
    `o 12 r 7(4) comment on one another's views`

-- src:1233 | (4) Where the experts testify as a panel, the Court may order that they give their views on the issues referred to them and comment on one another’s views.
@ref O 12 r 7(4) (src:1233)
GIVEN `the experts testify as a panel` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `o 12 r 7(4) a thing the panel might be ordered to do`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 7(4) the Court may order the experts to do this` MEANS
    IF `the experts testify as a panel`
    THEN
        CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `o 12 r 7(4) give their views on the issues referred to them` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 12 r 7(4) comment on one another's views` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the experts testify as a panel" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:1234 | (5) The Court may order cross‑examination and re‑examination of all or some of the experts in the panel in any sequence as the Court thinks appropriate, whether before or after the experts have testified as a panel.
@ref O 12 r 7(5) (src:1234)
GIVEN `the experts are in the panel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 7(5) the Court may order cross-examination and re-examination of all or some of the experts in the panel in any sequence` MEANS
    IF `the experts are in the panel`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "all or some of the experts in the panel"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:1235 | (6) The Court may give any other directions as are appropriate for the particular case.
@ref O 12 r 7(6) (src:1235)
GIVEN `the direction is appropriate for the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 12 r 7(6) the Court may give any other directions` MEANS
    IF `the direction is appropriate for the particular case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other directions as are appropriate for the particular case" [marginal-b]
